// What an end block stores at fp + 0: the returned value, or for a block that
// ends the function without one (a call that never returns) a zero, except in a
// function that returns a struct or union, where it is the pointer to the
// caller's object so the caller's copy of the result reads its own temporary.
ret_text(int e) {
  string txt = "0";
  if(e >= 0) {
    txt = retval_txt(e);
  } else {
    txt = ret_none();
  }
} return string txt;
